Z||000000||loren||01-14-2001||10:34 PM||||I need a set of dew strips. does anyone know<BR>where i can get some ?<BR>Could strips that are designed for other autos be adapted to fit a GT.<BR>Sure would appreciate any info.<P>Loren<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||01-14-2001||10:54 PM||||Welcome to the spot!!!!<P>Look in the Mall and/or do a search<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||12
Z||000002||ka4nkf||01-14-2001||11:00 PM||||I think they are still availible from GM, also the fiero store has them. I don't think any other auto strips will fit. Also they are not fun to put on.||||reg||1
Z||000003||pherder||01-14-2001||11:14 PM||||Go to this URL ... it has the answer ...<P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/002197.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/002197.html</A> <P>and the place to buy them from ...<P> <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsdirect.com/parts.cfm" TARGET=_blank>www.gmpartsdirect.com/parts.cfm</A> ||||reg||6
Z||000004||2birds||01-15-2001||10:19 PM||||I just got one from my local GM dealer today.  $30, cheaper than anyone else I've checked with, and no shipping charges.  Window switches were $15.  One day turnaround.<P>By the way, $30 is cheap.  The outer door dew strips for a 89 Z-24 Cavalier convertible are $195 each, and the rear side windows cost $95.  A friend of mine needs to replace all four outers on his.||||reg||1
Z||000005||286SE'S||01-17-2001||02:39 PM||||gmpartsdirect.com is the cheapest I found them. About $50 for the pair includes shipping. There is nothing that compares to a Fiero with new dew strips! They make the car look Factory fresh. This is the first thing you see when you get into the car and are worth the time to install. Rodney Dickmans dew strip tool is worth every penny and makes the job so easy.I have done 3 strips so far and here are some extra tips:<BR>Since the mirror has to come off, repaint it!<BR>I had a spare all ready to put on (planned ahead) Also those christmas tree door panel holders are probably going to break or lose some strength so have some spares ready. I put all new ones on and the panel is solid and door shuts quietly. There are about 9 per side. The door panel (and armrest)is so easy to clean when it is off. Try some softscrub cleanser for the tough spots. A simple mens double bladed shaver can be used on the carpet, it removes the fuzzies and really works. Just run it along the carpet with some pressure, cleaning the blade often. I used a product called Quick and Brite on the carpet. Looks almost new.||||reg||1
Z||000006||87GT||01-17-2001||04:22 PM||||Hi, I am trying to buy the wipes at gmpartsdirect.com and I filled in all the blanks for purchase and its asking me for my personal id #.  I am looking all over the site to figure out how to register so that I get one.  I cant figure out where to go. Is there some secret to this thing?  BTW, if I order 2 of each item number, will that be a set for each side of car? Or,is each item number a set for each window.  Hope I dont confuse anybody.  Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000007||Bob Englert||01-17-2001||06:53 PM||||You need 4 part numbers to get the inner and outer dew wipes for each side.  Each is a unique part number.<P><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000008||Lisa 86 2m4||01-17-2001||07:34 PM||||I just did mine last weekend, and what a job, but worth it. Everything 286SE's said is perfect!  But I got my wipes through the fierostore at $38 per outer wipe. The tool I used was sent to me by a forum member and is meant to be passed on, so if you're going to do it, let me know and I will send you the tool. An FYI, do not even start this project without that tool!! I spent 2 weeks with my door panels off! ||||reg||1
